---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { contact } from '../site';
---
<Base
  title="About — Pezi Labs"
  description="Pezi Labs is a one-person studio run by Tom Murphy, a user experience designer with more than 25 years of experience."
>
  <h1 style="margin-top:2.5rem;">About</h1>
  <p class="piece-lede">
    Pezi Labs is a one-person studio in New Hampshire. I'm Tom Murphy, and I run it.
  </p>

  <h2>Where I come from</h2>
  <p>
    I've spent more than 25 years in user experience design: at small startups, at large
    corporations, in my own freelance business, and most places in between. The thread has
    been the same the whole way. Find the real pain point, then use design and data to build
    a better system around it.
  </p>
  <p>
    Early on, the work was mostly the visual layer. Over time, the harder and more valuable
    part turned out to be understanding complex systems and the organizations that run them.
    I've always been comfortable straddling the line between engineering and product. The
    best results I've seen came from working closely across it, staying grounded in what the
    system can really do, and being willing to compromise to ship.
  </p>
  <p>
    AI changed the math. It now does a growing share of the building, which frees me to focus
    on what it can't do: sitting shoulder to shoulder with the people who have the problem,
    and shaping, scoping and delivering the tools they need to forge their own paths.
  </p>

  <h2>How the studio works</h2>
  <p>
    Right now that practice runs at home. I build
    <a href="/apps/">household applications</a>: small, specific apps for the people I live
    with, running privately on a computer in my house. Each one starts from a real need. Daily
    use shows which ones deserve more, and a few are becoming products.
  </p>
  <p>
    I build with AI agents as collaborators, and I write about what that's actually like in
    the <a href="/writing/">Journeyletter</a>. Every piece ends with a colophon that says
    which agents did what and what I did.
  </p>
  <p>
    The same practice is <a href="/services/">for hire</a>. I work with owner-run businesses
    on the problems behind their website.
  </p>

  <h2 id="contact">Get in touch</h2>
  <ul>
    {contact.email && <li><a href={`mailto:${contact.email}`}>{contact.email}</a></li>}
    {contact.linkedin && <li><a href={contact.linkedin}>LinkedIn</a>, for the full career history</li>}
    <li><a href={contact.github}>GitHub</a>, where Pezi Labs work lives</li>
  </ul>
  <p style="color:var(--ink-soft); font-size:0.9rem;">
    Pezi Labs LLC is a New Hampshire limited liability company. Looking for the
    Journeyletter's editorial rules? They're <a href="/writing/about/">here</a>.
  </p>
</Base>
